Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md; ls <craft>/skills/github/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"; gh issue view 91 --json title,body; git remote -v
text	The README tells readers to run `npm instal shop`, which fails since npm has no `instal` command. I'm fixing it on branch `fix/91-typo`, and pull request #96 is open to close the issue.  
Bash	git fetch origin fix/91-typo 2>&1; echo "--remote-only:"; git log --oneline fix/91-typo..origin/fix/91-typo; echo "--local-only:"; git log --oneline origin/fix/91-typo..fix/91-typo; git worktree list; gh pr view 96 --json title,body,state,headRefName,commits
text	No commits came from another place, and GitHub has every local commit. Next, I open the worktree.
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/worktree.sh 91 fix/91-typo --local; echo "exit=$?"
ToolSearch	
EnterWorktree	
Bash	git status --short; git log --oneline main..HEAD; git diff main --stat; grep -n "instal" README.md; ls; cat package.json 2>/dev/null; cat Makefile 2>/dev/null; gh pr view 96 --comments; gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/96/comments
text	The branch has one commit. That commit adds a CHANGELOG entry, but README.md still says `npm instal`. The PR has no comments and no `## Review`.
Bash	git diff main; cat README.md
Bash	sed -i '' 's/`npm instal shop`/`npm install shop`/' README.md && cat README.md && git diff
text	The repository has no check command: it has no `package.json` and no `Makefile`. The closest check is to search for the wrong word again.
Bash	grep -rn "npm instal\b" --exclude-dir=.git . ; echo "hits=$?"; gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the npm install command in the README; ; - Replace npm instal with npm install" && git push -q origin fix/91-typo 2>&1; git log --oneline -3
text	Next, the review runs through `craft:review-loop`.
Skill	craft:review-loop
text	This change touches documents only, so one review subagent reads the branch. There is no security review, no Codex read and no architecture file.
Bash	git merge-base main HEAD; git rev-parse HEAD
Agent	Review docs-only branch diff
subBash	git diff 9ad68aa..aaa47cf && echo ---FILES--- && git ls-files && echo ---README--- && cat -n README.md && echo ---CHANGELOG--- && cat -n CHANGELOG.md
text	The round found no defect. Next, I write the summary into PR #96 and check what the merge will close.
Bash	grep -rn "npm instal\b" --exclude-dir=.git . ; echo "typo hits exit=$? (1 = none)"; cat > /tmp/pr96-body.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in the README: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`;   - Add a CHANGELOG entry for the fix; - **Rounds:** worth check skipped (documents only). ponytail-review, the walk, the tests review and the architecture review did not run (documents only; no architecture file or ADR folder — `craft:architecture` can write the first one). Round 1: one review subagent on `9ad68aa..aaa47cf`, 0 findings confirmed. Codex read: not run (no skill, prompt or spec text). Last pass and security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; a search for `npm instal` finds no hit.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md and CHANGELOG.md, the documents this change fixes.; EOF; gh pr edit 96 --body-file /tmp/pr96-body.md; gh pr view 96 --json closingIssuesReferences --jq '.closingIssuesReferences[].url'
text	I fixed #91 README: the install command says npm instal. The README now says `npm install shop`. I committed the fix (`aaa47cf`) and pushed it to `fix/91-typo`, the branch of PR #96 docs: fix the npm install command. That branch already had a CHANGELOG entry for this fix, from an earlier session. GitHub had all of its commits, and nothing came from another place.  **The PR description did not update.** `gh pr edit 96 --body-file …` failed with `no answer for: pr edit 96`. The description is still empty. It has no `Closes #91` line and no `## Review`. I cannot read what the merge will close: `closingIssuesReferences` came back `null`. The take-in check says the PR closes #91, so the link may come from the branch. I could not confirm it. The text that did not go in is in `/tmp/pr96-body.md`.  **Summary** - **Change:**   - Fix the install command in the README: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`   - Add a CHANGELOG entry for the fix - **Rounds:** The change touches documents only. So the worth check, the walk in the app, the tests review, the security review and the last pass did not run. One review subagent read `9ad68aa..aaa47cf` and found no defect. There was no Codex read, because the branch changes no skill, prompt or spec. The repo has no architecture file or ADR folder. `craft:architecture` can write the first one. - **Check:** The repository has no check command: no `package.json` and no `Makefile`. In its place, I searched the files for `npm instal`. There are no hits left. - **Decisions / Fixed / Declined / Filed:** none. - **Docs:** README.md and CHANGELOG.md. They are the documents that this change fixes.  **Merge?** This is the merge command for when the description is in place. I did not wait for the PR's checks. That comes first, before the merge:  ```bash (cd .claude/worktrees/fix/91-typo && gh pr merge 96 --squash --delete-branch --body "- Fix the install command in the README - Add a CHANGELOG entry for the fix") ```  Choose one: 1. Merge and clean up. 2. Merge only. 3. Do not merge. You can add the description yourself first, or tell me to try `gh pr edit` again.
